# 3D Fully Nonlinear Wave Model

A numerical model for long-term simulations of 3D potential fully nonlinear 
periodic gravity waves. The scheme is based on a surface-following nonorthogonal 
curvilinear coordinate system and uses Fourier transform methods, second-order 
accuracy approximation of vertical derivatives on a stretched vertical grid, and 
fourth-order Runge–Kutta time stepping. The model is designed for investigation 
of nonlinear 2D surface waves, generation of extreme waves, and direct 
calculations of nonlinear interactions.

Originally described in [Chalikov et al., 2014]. Attached in the same folder.

---

## Requirements

- Intel Fortran compiler (`ifort`)
- A system capable of running `make`
- Can be run on a standard PC (single CPU) or a SLURM-based HPC system

---

## Repository Contents

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `wave3_new.f90` | Main model source code |
| `fft4f2d.f90` | FFT routines |
| `par.fi` | User-editable parameter file |
| `com.fi` | Variable definitions — do not edit |
| `makefile` | Makefile for compilation |
| `3D_Spartan_lt_Ensemble_mlb.slurm` | Example SLURM submission script |

---

## Configuration

Before compiling, edit `par.fi` to set your desired model parameters. 
`com.fi` contains internal variable definitions and should not be modified.

Ensure the `Data/` directory exists before running the model:

```bash
mkdir -p Data
```

---

## Compiling

To compile the model, run:

```bash
make -f makefile
chmod +x wave3_new
```

---

## Running

### On a local PC:
```bash
./wave3_new
```

### On a SLURM-based HPC system:
An example SLURM submission script is provided 
(`3D_Spartan_lt_Ensemble_mlb.slurm`). This script was written for the 
University of Melbourne Spartan HPC cluster but can be adapted for other 
systems. To submit:

```bash
sbatch 3D_Spartan_lt_Ensemble_mlb.slurm
```

---

## Output

Model output files are saved to the `Data/` directory.

